  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A line through the point \\((-a,0)\\) cuts from the second quadrant a triangular region with area \\(T.\\) The equation of the line is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(2Tx+a^2y+2aT=0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2Tx-a^2y+2aT=0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(2Tx+a^2y-2aT=0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(2Tx-a^2y-2aT=0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "none of these"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1964-p15.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let the \\(y\\)-intercept be \\(b.\\) The second-quadrant triangle has area \\(\\frac{ab}{2}=T,\\) so \\(b=\\frac{2T}{a}.\\) The intercept form is \\[\\frac{x}{-a}+\\frac{y}{\\frac{2T}{a}}=1.\\] Clearing denominators gives \\(2Tx-a^2y+2aT=0.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "If the positive \\(y\\)-intercept is \\(b,\\) then \\(\\frac12ab=T\\)",
        "Use the intercept form \\(-\\frac{x}{a}+\\frac{y}{b}=1\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
